feat: one-click unsubscribe — a deletion, not a flag

The privacy policy's promise gets its machinery. Confirmation now mints
a durable unsubscribeToken (stored in the clear on purpose: senders
must render each recipient's link, and it grants nothing but removal).
GET /api/unsubscribe deletes the subscriber document and removes the
Resend audience contact — neither store keeps the address — then lands
on /unsubscribed ('off the list and deleted — not parked'), excluded
from the i18n rewrite like /confirmed.

The digest template makes the link unforgettable at the type level:
unsubscribeUrl is a required prop, so a digest without it will not
compile. The footer echoes the shipped promise — 'one click, and it
works the first time.' The welcome template takes the link optionally;
the app's preview page renders a placeholder. Broadcasts must link our
endpoint, not Resend's hosted unsubscribe, which only suppresses — the
route comment records the contract. Privacy policy's warning comment
retired; its paragraph is now backed by code.

Verified: /api/unsubscribe 400s without a token, /unsubscribed renders,
217 tests, tsc, production build.

